WEBVTT

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.440
- Gotcha!
- Gotcha!

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.230
<i>Summer. It's the season of love.</i>

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.360
Stop it!

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.200
<i>Is burning a young lady's bare body
the sun's mischief?</i>

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.210
<i>Is the quivering of asphalt
a heat haze mirage?</i>

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.500
<i>A boy and girl
bare their hearts to each other</i>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.050
<i>and are invited to take the next step
in a male-female relationship.</i>

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.760
<i>The curtain comes up
on a summer vacation like that.</i>

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.010
<i>Half a month has passed!</i>

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.020
<i>During that time,
nothing in particular has happened.</i>

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.020
AUGUST

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.440
I screwed up.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.150
I totally screwed up.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.490
SHOPPING
FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.370
Was that a sigh?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.960
If you sigh like that,
happiness will flee in all directions.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:30.960
AI HAYASAKA
WANTS TO GET SOAKED

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.050
President Shirogane
says he's at home right now,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.510
so if you loiter around outside,
you may see him.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.350
Don't talk silly, Hayasaka.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.470
As if I would engage in stalker-like—

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.640
He says he's at home?

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.020
Hayasaka, since when have you been
in contact with the president?

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.480
Oh, I'm not.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.730
He was grumbling about it on Twitter.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.990
Twitter?

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.610
What's that? No, I've heard of it!

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.030
Twitter...

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.910
I think Miss Fujiwara does it.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:10.410
DICTIONARY

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.410
Twitter... Twitter...

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.410
Well, I'm going to take a bath.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:14.920
RESERVED

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.960
Again?

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.920
FEMALE EMPLOYEES'
BATHROOM

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.920
She gets to do that?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.060
There.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.570
SPLASH

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.690
FSSS

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.710
Hayasaka! Come quick!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:54.920
Wh-What is it?

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.040
The Internet is broken!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.460
It must be the major incident
of the century.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.380
So, I tried to start doing that thing,
you know, Twitter...

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:07.890
USER NAME
EMAIL ADDRESS
I AGREE TO THE TERMS
OF SERVICE.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.890
but the letters are garbled!

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.890
The letters are not garbled.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.890
Password.
Can I use my bank password?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:11.680
No.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.520
<i>Hopeless at I.T.</i>

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.980
HOPELESS AT I.T.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.980
<i>When it comes to technology,
Kaguya prefers to be analog.</i>

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:20.030
<i>She can do mental arithmetic,
but cant use a calculator.</i>

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:24.110
<i>When she looks into something, she'll use
a map or encyclopedia instead of googling.</i>

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.110
ENCYCLOPEDIA

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.330
<i>She does use the Internet once in a while
to check the weather or news headlines,</i>

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.250
<i>but never leaves the confines
of the search engine site's top page.</i>

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:36.130
<i>She's about as tech-savvy as the old man
who runs the candy shop.</i>

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:36.130
YAMADA STORE

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.130
Like this?

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.880
Yes. Now you have an account,
Lady Kaguya.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.890
MIYUKI SHIROGANE
CHIKA FUJIWARA
YU ISHIGAMI

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.890
I printed out the accounts
of the other student council members.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.220
For example,
this is the secretary's account.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:51.390
I WENT TO DUBAI

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:51.390
I WENT TO CALIFORNIA

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.810
She clearly spends a great deal of time
tweeting and no time at all studying.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.730
I WENT TO BALI

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.730
I WENT TO HAWAII

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.190
All she does is travel abroad.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.110
And this anime icon is the treasur—

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.480
Not interested.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.320
The best thing to do is play around
with it until you're used to it.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.780
Okay.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.870
Well, I'm going back to my bath.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.830
This job is exhausting.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:22.880
The only way I can take it
is by washing my fatigue away like this.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.630
Lady Kaguya doesn't understand.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.140
She should appreciate me more.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.060
Hayasaka! Come quick!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:32.890
Jeez.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.850
Lady Kaguya,
would you stop barging in on—

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.270
I've been banned from Twitter!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.270
I'm surprised you even know
about being banned.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.280
THIS ACCOUNT'S TWEETS
ARE PROTECTED.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.280
L-Look!

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.740
I can't see it! Why?
Did I do something wrong?

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.030
President Shirogane
has a protected account.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:50.910
Protected?

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.620
It's because some trolls will flame you
no matter what you post.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.040
This goes to show that the president
is on his toes about privacy.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.710
My main account is protected, too.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.920
You'd better be very careful, too,
Lady Kaguya.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.420
In other words,

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.670
think of your account as your house.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:10.300
With normal accounts,
the front door is wide open,

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.560
so visitors can come and go
as they please.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.350
But cautious people
keep their front door locked,

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.060
and only visitors
who are given a key can come in.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.860
Then, where do you get a key?

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:24.940
That's simple.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.190
FOLLOW

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.190
LIKES

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.190
If you click this "Follow" button,

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:31.200
a request for approval
will be sent to President Shirogane.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.490
If he agrees,
you'll then be able to see his tweets.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.960
I imagine he'd okay any request, as long as
their profile shows they go to Shuchiin.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.920
But... But I... But I...

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.340
There's no way I can do that!

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.670
After all, it would mean...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.840
<i>President! Please open up!</i>

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.310
<i>I want to know more about you!</i>

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.310
REQUESTING APPROVAL
FOR A FOLLOW

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:59.060
<i>I want to know what you think about
and what you usually do!</i>

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:59.060
BAM BAM

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:03.230
<i>You want to know about me that badly?</i>

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:07.940
<i>You're that interested
in my 140-character monologues?</i>

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.950
<i>That's cute.</i>

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:16.870
APPROVED

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.030
Like that, right?

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.870
Is this a new kind of stupidity?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.460
You really think
of the most useless things.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.580
Are you mad at me, Hayasaka?

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.540
Mad? More like I'm wondering...

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.250
how long you're going to make me
stand around half-naked.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:28.630
Sorry.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.470
If you won't do it, Lady Kaguya, I—

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:31.220
Wait! Wait!

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.380
Hold on!

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.600
I'll do it when I'm good and ready!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.150
FOLLOW

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.150
LIKES

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:52.110
<i>I wonder what the president
tweets about.</i>

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.370
<i>What is he doing? What does he like?</i>

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.080
<i>How is he spending his summer?</i>

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:01.910
<i>But...</i>

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.870
<i>But...</i>

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.550
That's it! I'll protect my account, too!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.630
- Then, if the president follows me—
- Wake up and smell the coffee.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.140
You've never succeeded
with that pattern before. Not even once.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.140
In the end,
she wasn't able to send the request.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:28.150
Lady Kaguya is stubborn to a fault.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.400
They both are hopeless.

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:35.530
If either were open about their feelings,
they could both be happy.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.530
But I envy them.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:43.410
I wish I loved someone like that.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:50.800
As if...

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.880
Hayasaka! Come quick!

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.180
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.720
<i>None.</i>

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:02.930
KAGUYA AND SHIROGANE DIDN'T MEET UP

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.390
Please! Enough already!

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.940
CLICK CLICK

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.940
HER TYPING IS VERY FAST

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:11.150
CHIKA FUJIWARA
REALLY WANTS TO EAT IT

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.940
Japan!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.570
I loved Egypt.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.950
I wish we could've stayed there
a little longer.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:22.200
The ta'amiya and kushari were delicious!

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.580
You're just thinking about food!

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.000
Maybe you wanted to stay longer, Sis,

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.840
but I couldn't wait to get back to Japan!

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:32.960
Why?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.720
After all...

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.520
<i>My name is Saburo Odajima.</i>

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.480
<i>I'm an insignificant middle manager.</i>

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.480
RAMEN

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.480
HAKATA TENRYU

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.850
<i>My hobby is frequenting ramen shops.</i>

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.980
TENRYU RAMEN

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:53.980
Welcome.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.490
<i>I came to a neighborhood shop today.</i>

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>The most popular item on the menu
is pork bone broth ramen...</i>

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.740
<i>but that's not for me.</i>

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.950
<i>I get the inconspicuous one
all the way at the end.</i>

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.500
Soy sauce pork bone. Thin.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.080
How about the noodles?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.130
Firm.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.880
<i>That is this shop's optimum combination.</i>

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.630
<i>The way I ordered
shows I'm in the know.</i>

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:17.630
Welcome.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.140
It smells wonderful!

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.140
GLOW

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.100
<i>Well, well, a cute customer...</i>

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.720
<i>Maybe she wandered in
thinking this was a cake shop.</i>

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.640
What can I get you?

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.390
Um,

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:30.860
soy sauce pork bone ramen, thin broth!

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:32.520
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.900
<i>Did a girl like this suddenly calculate
this shop's optimum combination?</i>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.900
OPTIMUM COMBINATION

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.860
<i>Is it a coincidence? No.</i>

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:45.160
<i>This isn't the kind of shop a young woman
would enter alone this late at night.</i>

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:45.160
RAMEN

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.960
<i>Could this woman be one of "my people"?</i>

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.290
MY PEOPLE

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:52.840
What about the noodles?

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.420
Um,

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.840
super-firm!

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.670
FSSS

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.420
<i>Super-firm?</i>

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.930
<i>Like a sheep,
she chose the fad level of firmness.</i>

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:05.180
<i>She's just an average girl after all.
I worried for nothing.</i>

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.180
<i>I overestimated her.</i>

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:09.560
Here you go.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:14.940
<i>All right, then. I'll teach this girl
the real way to eat ramen.</i>

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:18.190
<i>First, you note the scent
of the soup itself.</i>

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.450
<i>The idea is to appreciate
each scent in turn</i>

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:24.700
<i>starting from the fragrant
red pickled ginger.</i>

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:28.450
<i>Of course, the owner is fully aware of that.</i>

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.960
<i>I'm delighted at his consideration,
placing the ginger farthest away.</i>

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.960
<i>Next, the taste.</i>

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.300
<i>Letting the air mix in while you taste it.</i>

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:42.800
<i>I use my brain completely,
sharpening my senses of smell and taste.</i>

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.850
<i>And then, the noodles.</i>

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.100
<i>I bite off a small amount,
as if making sure of the flavor,</i>

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:52.770
<i>and enjoy it as it slides down.</i>

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:53.730
Here you go.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.110
Thank you for the meal!

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.360
<i>Finally, the chaser.</i>

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.650
<i>In order to enjoy the delicate flavors,</i>

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:05.740
<i>I drink water to wash away the soy and salt
on my tongue, resetting my palate.</i>

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.620
<i>This makes all the difference.</i>

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.410
<i>This is one set.</i>

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.120
<i>Repeating the set over and over
is what we call the "water cycle."</i>

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.630
<i>Now, what about you, young lady?</i>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.630
<i>Mini-ramen?</i>

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.090
Little bits. Little bits. Little bits.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.760
<i>She really is just an ordinary girl.</i>

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.390
GOBBLE...

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.390
<i>Looks like she's enjoying it.</i>

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.890
<i>Well, I can't really look down on her.</i>

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.940
<i>Mini-ramen,
where you eat it all in each bite,</i>

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:39.400
<i>is the ultimate form
of the "one is all" philosophy after all.</i>

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:43.150
Little bits. Little bits. Little bits.
Little bits! Little bits. Little bits!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:43.150
<i>But by taking little bites like that,
the noodles will stretch out and swell up.</i>

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.160
<i>Swell up?</i>

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:48.160
<i>Super-firm! Super-firm! Super-firm!</i>

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.160
<i>Is that why she said, "Super-firm"?</i>

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.540
<i>Did this girl calculate
that the noodles would stretch out?</i>

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.460
Slurp, slurp, slurp!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.880
<i>Moreover, using that small utensil
is perfect for mini-ramen!</i>

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:57.920
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.710
<i>If this was all calculated...</i>

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.260
<i>The metro's four ramen kings...</i>

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.920
<i>Jinbocho's Mashimashi Mama,</i>

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:05.510
<i>the Hermit of Sugamo,</i>

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.760
<i>even J. Suzuki of Koenji...</i>

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.760
THE METRO AREA'S
BIG FOUR RAMEN KINGS

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.760
JINBOCHO'S
MASHIMASHI MAMA

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.760
J. SUZUKI OF KOENJI
HERMIT OF SUGAMO

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:13.180
<i>So, she possesses the sense
of situational assessment</i>

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:15.520
<i>equivalent to the monsters
of the ramen world!</i>

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.520
SAN OF SHIBUYA

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.150
<i>Not yet.</i>

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.280
<i>That's right. She's not there yet.</i>

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:22.530
<i>It's kind of sad.</i>

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:27.200
<i>It's the wall that can't be overcome,
and it's owing to being a woman.</i>

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.700
<i>- Garlic!
- Garlic!</i>

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:33.450
<i>Unfortunately, avoiding that scent
pegs her as a wannabe ramen connoisseur.</i>

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:35.960
<i>She's a fake!</i>

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.470
<i>Looks like she finished
eating the ingredients.</i>

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:45.670
<i>What is she gonna do now?</i>

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:48.010
<i>There's no more to spoon out!</i>

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:50.220
<i>What's she gonna do?</i>

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.850
<i>Is she gonna go for it?</i>

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:53.930
<i>She's gonna go for it?</i>

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:57.270
CRUNCH

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.100
<i>She went for it!</i>

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.690
<i>She overcame the wall of womanhood!</i>

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.820
<i>I have to give her props!
She's earned my respect!</i>

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:09.200
<i>She's definitely "my people"!</i>

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.830
<i>A ramen connoisseur!</i>

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:17.710
<i>Don't tell me!</i>

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.000
<i>Even the soup?</i>

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.210
<i>Too much salt!</i>

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.800
<i>You're drinking garlic, too!</i>

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:28.930
<i>But...</i>

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:31.260
<i>It looks delicious!</i>

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:33.350
<i>...there was a time in my life, too!</i>

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.220
<i>Thank you for the meal!</i>

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.850
<i>When did I become such an old man?</i>

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:44.320
GULP GULP

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.320
<i>That's it! Run!</i>

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:47.490
<i>That youth is the radiance I lost!</i>

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.700
<i>I'm young and starving!</i>

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.540
<i>Keep running!</i>

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.330
AHHH

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.330
POLISHED IT OFF

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.960
Thank you!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:03.960
<i>Boom!</i>

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:05.920
You...

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.430
COOL

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.760
<i>Result of today's ramen match...</i>

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:18.930
RESULT OF TODAY'S RAMEN MATCH:

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.100
<i>Fujiwara wins.</i>

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.930
FUJIWARA WINS

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.440
WHERE IS YOUR SWITCH?

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.940
My ramen switch is on!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.860
MIYUKI SHIROGANE
WANTS TO SEE YOU

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.940
<i>Since summer vacation began,</i>

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.030
<i>three weeks have passed.</i>

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.200
<i>Nothing of note
has happened during that time.</i>

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:39.080
Days of studying, working, eating,
taking a bath, sleeping, and that's all.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.710
This has become
a boring summer vacation.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.960
<i>The festival at the end of vacation
is the only plan</i>

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.960
<i>he and Kaguya made to see each other.</i>

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:51.720
<i>Other than that,
they haven't exchanged a single text,</i>

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:52.970
<i>let alone go out together.</i>

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.720
<i>The high hurdle of asking the other person
to go out and do something fun</i>

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.470
<i>is still insurmountable.</i>

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.980
It wasn't supposed to be like this.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:08.730
I wonder what Shinomiya's doing now.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:12.240
It wasn't supposed to be like this.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.070
Why has it come to this?

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.240
The reason, Lady Kaguya...

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:23.250
is that, all your plans are based on the premise
that the president is going to invite you.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.250
SUMMER VACATION PLANS
FOR KAGUYA

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.750
You've been too naive.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.800
Hayasaka, why are you looking
at your lady's notebook

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:29.130
so brazenly and without permission?

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.840
Why don't you just ask him
to do something?

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.720
Don't be ridiculous!

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:36.970
It'd look like I wanted to do something
for fun with the president!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.850
That's exactly right.
I mean, you're not even refuting me.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.600
TO: KAGUYA SHINOMIYA

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.600
Shi-no-mi-ya...

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:46.150
What-are-you-doing...

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.110
DELETE THIS MAIL?

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.110
SAVE

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.110
DELETE

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.110
Am I some blushing girl?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.110
WHAP

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.700
Write, delete, write, delete!

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:56.870
What is this, your first love?

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.620
<i>It is his first love.</i>

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.620
AUGUST

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.580
That's it! I'm done! I'm through!

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.120
SUBJECT: OCTOPUS
LOOK! A LIVE OCTOPUS!!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.750
FROM: SHIROGANE
I WAS TRYING TO TELL YOU SOMETHING
AS YOU HUNG UP THE PHONE

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.750
LOOKS LIKE TONIGHT WILL GET
PRETTY COLD, SO BE WARM
AND GO TO SLEEP
GOOD NIGHT

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.880
No matter how much you read that,
it won't make new messages appear.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:17.260
Did that message make you so happy
that you've saved it all this time?

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.010
The president's first text to you.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:22.220
You were thrilled when he made
the first move there, weren't you?

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.230
You can't forget it, huh?

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.270
Get off my back!

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.560
I don't think that at all,

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.530
so stop trying to analyze my heart!

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.490
I'm going out.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.830
Where are you going, Bro?

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.450
Grocery shopping for dinner.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.290
In your school uniform?

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.080
Well, I may stop at school on the way.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.460
The school isn't on the way.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:01.850
<i>What I'm doing now doesn't make any sense.</i>

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:08.060
<i>But I thought, "What if," and...</i>

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.340
Nice and cool.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.480
I want to see him...

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:52.770
STUDENT COUNCIL ROOM

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:05.830
Well, of course not...

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:22.970
<i>- I wish summer vacation weren't so long.
- I wish summer vacation weren't so long.</i>

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.470
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH: NONE

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.730
BECAUSE THEY DIDN'T MEET UP

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:05.450
<i>I don't have any summer memories.</i>

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.280
Look! Look!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.830
<i>But that's not a problem.</i>

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:15.000
<i>I've never gone on a family vacation.</i>

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:16.710
<i>But that's okay...</i>

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:20.170
<i>because everyone treats me
like I'm special.</i>

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:24.220
<i>I've never gone to see
a fireworks display.</i>

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.180
<i>But that's all right...</i>

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:31.220
<i>because even the little lights
I see from out my window are pretty.</i>

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:37.230
FROM: MISS FUJIWARA

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:37.230
LET'S MEET UP IN FRONT OF
THE MOAI STATUE TOMORROW!
I CAN'T WAIT!!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:37.230
<i>I've never gone shopping
with a group of friends.</i>

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:39.320
Yeah. Like this one?

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:41.610
<i>So, I felt a mix
of anxiety and anticipation.</i>

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.530
<i>But it would be okay.</i>

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:47.820
<i>The people I was going with
were good people.</i>

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:49.450
<i>They were all very nice.</i>

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.160
<i>But it's okay.</i>

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:56.870
<i>I'm used to it.</i>

00:21:57.170 --> 00:22:01.050
<i>I can't do what I want in this life.</i>

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:06.430
FROM: KAGUYA
SUBJECT: TOMORROW - I'M SORRY.
I CAN'T GO SHOPPING TOMORROW.

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:06.880
"My father suddenly summoned me
to the main house in Kyoto, so I have to go.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:11.510
Don't worry about me. All of you
should go on and have fun, okay?"

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:12.640
That's what she says.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.270
What should we do?

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:16.640
In this case...

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:18.520
we put it off!

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:21.770
The whole point
is for all of us to go together.

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.070
Good! You're right!

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.030
I'll call Kei and let her know.

00:22:27.820 --> 00:22:28.910
<i>That's right.</i>

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:31.080
<i>I'm blessed.</i>

00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:36.410
<i>I've got friends and a distinguished family
that anyone would envy.</i>

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:40.170
<i>I'm blessed with a resourcefulness
that anyone would be jealous of.</i>

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.920
<i>Anyone would conclude that the amount
of my happiness and sorrow are about the same.</i>

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:50.260
<i>So, blessed as I am,
it's only logical that I should suck it up.</i>

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:55.470
F-Father!

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:57.980
Oh, you're here?

00:22:58.230 --> 00:22:59.350
Good.

00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:08.360
He summoned you
all the way here for that?

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.990
Drop dead, asshole.

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:15.740
<i>My father has never said
"good night" to me.</i>

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:18.500
<i>I don't remember him
ever saying "See you later,"</i>

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:21.500
<i>"Good job" or "I love you" to me either.</i>

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:24.750
<i>But it doesn't hurt my feelings.</i>

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:27.920
<i>Because it's always been this way.</i>

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:31.010
<i>By this point, nothing he does
makes me feel one way or the other.</i>

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:32.510
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:34.930
<i>In deference to my family's status,</i>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:38.520
<i>people around here
behave a certain way toward me...</i>

00:23:39.440 --> 00:23:41.150
<i>with great caution...</i>

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:43.150
<i>as if there's no problem...</i>

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:47.530
<i>like I'm a creepy
traditional Japanese doll.</i>

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:53.780
<i>But I don't mind.</i>

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:57.790
<i>After all, I'm going
to a fireworks festival tomorrow.</i>

00:23:55.160 --> 00:23:59.580
I CAN'T HEAR
THE FIREWORKS, PART 1
